Title: Burp Suite - First Intercepted HTTP Request

Date: 2026-10-02

Goal
----
Verify that Burp Suite successfully intercepts browser traffic.

Setup
-----
Burp Suite running on Kali Linux.

Browser traffic configured to pass through Burp proxy.

Burp listener:

127.0.0.1:8080

Procedure
---------
1. Opened Burp Suite.
2. Enabled:

Proxy -> Intercept -> ON

3. Opened:

http://neverssl.com

4. Burp intercepted request:

GET / HTTP/1.1
Host: neverssl.com

Observation
-----------
Initial intercepted traffic was:

POST / HTTP/1.1
Host: ocsp.r2m04.amazontrust.com

This was not website traffic.

It was an OCSP request used by Firefox to verify certificate status.

A normal web request appeared after opening:

http://neverssl.com

Captured Request
----------------

GET / HTTP/1.1
Host: neverssl.com
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64; rv:140.0) Gecko/20100101 Firefox/140.0
Accept: text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8
Accept-Language: en-US,en;q=0.5
Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br
Connection: keep-alive
Upgrade-Insecure-Requests: 1

Key Headers
-----------
Host
    Target website.

User-Agent
    Browser and operating system information.

Accept
    Preferred response content types.

Accept-Language
    Preferred response language.

Accept-Encoding
    Supported compression methods.

Exercise
--------
Modified:

User-Agent

Example:

User-Agent: BurpLearning

Forwarded modified request through Burp.

Result
------
Successfully intercepted and inspected a real HTTP request.

Learned how browser requests appear in raw HTTP format.

Confirmed that Burp is working correctly.
